+## Amendment, 2026-09-02: three more first-class directories
+
+Founder word, 2026-09-02 (recommendation put to him during the lane-alignment round; he
+accepted). The four Diátaxis directories stand, and three directories the estate already
+depends on are named first-class rather than migrated:
+
+- `docs/demo/` and `docs/onboarding/` — the LAW 32 pre-push gate requires
+  `docs/demo/<name>.md` and `docs/onboarding/<name>.md` at those exact paths for every
+  `feat(<name>)` push, and tier-1 Demo Standard pages already sit there on main.
+- `docs/runbooks/` — the runbook-per-PR rule (R54) writes there.
+
+A migration into the four directories plus a rewrite of the gate paths was the
+alternative and was rejected: it buys nothing a reader or a buyer sees.
+
+The unchanged half of the rule is the half that was being broken: **every page, in any of
+these seven directories, gets an `mkdocs.yml` nav row in the same commit.** A page off
+the nav never renders in the portal and does not exist.
+
 ## What we are NOT adopting, and why
 
 **AGENTS.md is not a documentation standard, and we already have it.** It is a community
